---

### UX Rationale (Updated)
1. **Contextual Actions:** 
   - **Draft Email**: Clicking "Draft Email" on a specific contact row will open a modal/interface showing a custom drafted email pre-populated for *that specific contact*. The user will be able to review the auto-generated email, make any manual edits, and then either send or discard it from this stage.
   - **Slack It**: Same concept. Clicking "Slack It" on a contact's row sends the approval request to Slack prepopulated with *that specific target*. Both actions live next to the contact. We will remove the generic "Send Email" / "Slack it" from the top-level table row actions since it is ambiguous when there are multiple contacts.
2. **Inline Editability:** A persistent edit icon (✏️) or an interactive, frameless input structure will exist on every field (Name, Title, Email, Website) across all contacts. Changes to these inputs will instantly save to the DB array so the user never loses edits.
   - **Hunter Re-validation**: If the user edits an *Email* field, we will trigger a backend call to re-verify the new email using the Hunter API, updating the Valid/Invalid badge dynamically.
3. **Valid/Invalid Checks**: If an email is Invalid, the action buttons will grey out to prevent sending bouncy emails unless the user steps in and edits the email manually.
